From c0b6945490f5999847c895fbb5698f25176fff27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 07:08:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Replay retained Bezier ranges through exact SVG graph
 metadata

Exporting an ellipse cut by a line and chamfered failed: the chamfer
meets the ellipse at an algebraic parameter, leaving a RetainedBezier
fragment (native source and exact range in its own chart) that the graph
could not encode. Graph tag 32 writes the source as a native record and
both boundaries as parameter references. Import checks the source family
and that the range is ordered inside [0, 1], then rebuilds the piece
with the splitter that created it. Older readers reject the new tag.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
